## 6. Ease of cleaning and health-inspection readiness

### Common chain standard

Regardless of city, specify:

- 304 stainless food-contact and splash surfaces;
- continuously welded, coved internal corners;
- no exposed screw heads or hollow seams in food zones;
- equipment on sealed plinths or movable casters;
- sufficient clearance for cleaning where units are not sealed;
- removable drip trays, filters, burner rings and strainers;
- self-draining floors and accessible grease traps;
- separate handwashing and warewashing facilities;
- automatic oven-cleaning records;
- daily hood-filter and grease-cup checks;
- documented duct-cleaning and fire-suppression schedules;
- colour-coded cleaning tools and chemical controls.

### Regulatory differences that affect equipment selection

**Singapore:** Choose equipment and layouts that facilitate grease-trap and exhaust-system maintenance. Automated HACCP records and easily documented cleaning cycles will support a relatively formal licensing environment.

**Bangkok:** Worktables used for preparation or cooking must be at least **60 cm above the floor** and use easily cleanable material. Inspection guidance emphasizes smooth, non-rusting, non-toxic and corrosion-resistant surfaces, adequate lighting and clean ventilation equipment (https://laws.anamai.moph.go.th/th/ministry-rule/download/?did=204266&id=71870&reload; https://foodsanitation.bangkok.go.th/assets/uploads/document/document/20210122_32302.pdf).

**Manila:** Equipment must be designed, fabricated and installed for easy cleaning without health hazards. The Sanitation Code requires utensil washing in warm water at **120°F/49°C** with soap or detergent, followed by an approved bactericidal treatment (https://elibrary.judiciary.gov.ph/thebookshelf/showdocs/26/15313). Dishwashers must therefore provide validated wash and sanitizing performance appropriate to local rules.

**Jakarta:** Use smooth, easy-clean surfaces and separate handwashing and equipment-washing stations. Mechanical smoke extraction must not contaminate or disturb surrounding areas. Certification procedures are evolving: Jakarta’s older 2015 hygiene-certificate procedure was revoked in 2026 because authority shifted under the newer integrated licensing framework. Local counsel or the licensing consultant should confirm the current approval route before opening.

